Additionally, the increased slurry carryover led to frequent overloading of the filtrate receivers and contributed to premature wear of internal components within the filtrate pumps.
The combined impact of these issues was increased maintenance requirements and unplanned downtime, negatively affecting overall Paste Plant reliability and productivity.', N'Extend disc filter sector bag life', N'10311', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/10906.jpeg', N'The existing disc filter bags were oversized relative to the sectors, resulting in excess material that caused creasing when vacuum pressure was applied. These creases created high-stress points, leading to premature wear and the frequent development of holes.
Due to the high failure rate, filter bags required frequent replacement. To mitigate excessive downtime and maintain Paste Plant throughput, filters were often kept in service despite the presence of holes in the bags.
This situation highlighted a need for improved bag fitment to enhance durability, reduce maintenance frequency, and support more reliable filter operation.', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/10906.jpeg', N'A sector was sent to Micronics to develop and fit-test a custom bag design tailored to our disc filters. Following successful testing, a batch of the new bags was delivered to site and installed on Disc Filter #2.
The new bag design demonstrated clear improvements, including a tighter fit, reduced creasing, and minimized contact with the deflector blades. At the same time, Disc Filters #1 and #3 were re-bagged using the existing (old-style) bags, allowing for a direct performance comparison under similar operating conditions.
After several months of operation, the new bag design on Filter #2 exhibited a significantly longer service life compared to the old-style bags used on Filters #1 and #3.
Based on these results, the site will transition to the new bag design as the standard, with inventory updated accordingly and the old-style bags phased out. This improvement is expected to reduce maintenance frequency, minimize downtime associated with bag change-outs, and decrease wear-related ', NULL, N'While the new-style bags are still subject to wear over time and can develop holes or crease if not installed correctly, they have improved overall performance.
The improved fit and reduced failure rate have contributed meaningfully to increased Paste Plant availability, supporting more stable operation and reduced downtime compared to the previous bag design.', N'Vendor packages from commissioning are not always perfect. Things can always be improved.', 5000000, 3, N'Access to electrical panel should remain free and accessible going forward', '2026-06-27T00:00:00.000', '2026-06-28T13:37:58.000', N'1010749', NULL, NULL);
