Impact - unplanned down time due to bearing failures  Issues was found during lubrication inspections. ', N'improve equipment health', N'0', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/11152.jpeg', N'The filter belt contains 60 lubrication points that are supplied through a grease system utilizing diverter blocks. With the existing design, grease must travel significant distances through distribution points before reaching some bearings. This made it difficult to verify that each lubrication point was receiving an adequate amount of grease. As a result, some bearings experienced insufficient lubrication, leading to increased wear, premature bearing failures, unplanned maintenance, and reduced equipment reliability.', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/11152.jpeg', N'Individual automatic lubricators were installed directly on each bearing, eliminating grease lines and diverter blocks. This provides a direct and reliable grease supply, with adjustable lubrication rates based on bearing demand. The clear lubricator housing allows easy monitoring during inspections and identifies when replacement is required. Benefits include improved bearing reliability, reduced maintenance, and less downtime caused by lubrication-related failures.', NULL, N'yes, with this new lubrication system, bearing failures will be greatly reduced ', N'utilising lubrication best practice is the best path ', 94545, 3, N'Reduced business continuity risks through elimination of obsolete technology', '2026-07-12T00:00:00.000', '2026-07-13T13:00:24.000', N'81057857', NULL, NULL);
