', N'Automate water spray control for RCT Operations', N'10260', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/12171.jpeg', N'•	The mine is dry and dusty. Mucking with a scoop generates heavy dust; water spray is used to wet the area and suppress it.
•	Placing a controlled spray system near an active draw point traditionally meant running dedicated power (and/or fiber) thousands of feet through the drift — high material and labour cost.
•	Continuous spray coated autonomous scoop cameras with mist, reducing visibility for the surface operator and interrupting mucking.
•	Autonomous mucking depends on the LTE signal. Microhard NMDs already monitor signal across the mine, but there was no unit close to the active mucking location with its metrics easily accessible on the process HMI.
•	Conventional PLC setups each carried a unique IP and a local program, so a field swap required an automation technician with a laptop.
', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/12171.jpeg', N'Power and connectivity — no dedicated utility runs
•	Power is taken from existing infrastructure via a Geo-Beacon 48 VDC tap on the LTE cable (power only).
•	Each unit is built for either source: a 120 V supply or a 48 VDC-to-24 VDC converter. All controls run at 24 V, and a simple wiring change by the electrician, at install, selects the source.
•	Communication is over the LTE radiating cable: the Microhard modem connects to the LTE/radiating cable, and the PLC connects to the modem by Ethernet.
•	On one 450 m LTE run, a box was powered and connected at roughly the 425 m mark off a Geo-Beacon tap — running reliably with zero dedicated power or fiber pulled to that location. This is the core saving: thousands of feet of cable, plus the labour to hang it, eliminated.
Identical, swappable boxes
', NULL, N'YES - Problem was solved.
Dust suppression was greatly improved and the automatic function of the water spray prevented any detriment to camera image.

', N'•	Proven reliability: the lead unit has run six months without any issues. •	Eliminated dedicated power/fiber runs and the associated labour at the deployed locations, using Geo-Beacon power and the radiating-LTE signal. Negligible load — each box draws roughly ¼ amp total, so a single LTE line easily carries one or two units. •	Faster field swaps and quick HMI fallback modes reduce downtime; flow, valve, and motion diagnostics give the team eyes on the system from surface. •	Removed autonomous-haulage interruptions caused by water on the camera, while adding LTE signal/uptime monitoring at critical locations. •	Moved from a one-off build to a repeatable, schedule-ready kit.', 0, NULL, N'Eliminado a utilização do trabalho em altura, tempo de aproximadamente 06:00h na mobilização, montagem e desmontagem de andaime, esforço excessivo.', '2026-08-31T00:00:00.000', '2026-09-04T14:45:09.000', N'81025074', NULL, NULL);
', N'Prevent damage to zero speed and belt switches', N'10260', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/12172.jpeg', N'The cable was run in a way that made it easy to snag and relied on the maintenance personnel to make sure it remained clear of the carriage during movement.
Damage was regularly occurring to the cable, which would take down the conveyer as this circuit was part of 2 critical sensors.
We needed a system where the cable could move freely, yet remain protected and secure.', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/12172.jpeg', N'Attaching the cable to festoon trolleys that rode on a length of messenger cable that spanned the length of possible carriage travel.
This keeps the cable up and free from harm, while allowing movement of the carriage and not impeding maintenance work.', NULL, N'Yes - the problem was solved.
Industrial mechanics gave very positive feedback on the solution.
The festoons move freely up and down the messenger cable.', N'Effective method of cable protection.', 0, NULL, N'Higher visibility of pedestrians using the crosswalk.', '2026-03-30T00:00:00.000', '2026-09-04T14:59:13.000', N'81025074', NULL, NULL);
', '2026-09-03T00:00:00.000', '2026-09-04T16:55:02.000', N'81053608', NULL, NULL);
